# Copy this file to `.env` (same directory) and replace the value below with your
# real connection string. `.env` is gitignored — never commit the real secret.
#
# Prisma auto-loads packages/db/.env for CLI commands (generate/migrate/etc.).
#
# ── Hosted Postgres (Neon / Supabase) notes ────────────────────────────────────
# SSL: managed providers require TLS. Append `?sslmode=require` to the URL
#      (Neon/Supabase strings usually already include it). Without it you'll get
#      a connection error.
#
# DIRECT vs POOLED — this matters:
#   • Migrations (migrate deploy/dev) MUST use a DIRECT connection. They take
#     advisory locks and run DDL that a transaction-mode pooler (PgBouncer /
#     Supavisor) breaks. Use the direct/non-pooled host for DATABASE_URL now.
#       - Neon:     the host WITHOUT `-pooler` in it.
#       - Supabase: the "Direct connection" string (port 5432).
#   • Serverless runtime (Phase 5) may prefer a POOLED connection to survive
#     many short-lived connections. If you switch DATABASE_URL to a pooled host,
#     add `?pgbouncer=true` (disables prepared statements) and give Prisma a
#     separate `directUrl` (direct host) for migrations. We'll wire `directUrl`
#     into schema.prisma in Phase 5 if/when we go pooled.
#
# Free-tier connection limits are low (Neon ~100 but auto-suspends; Supabase
# direct ~60). Keep a single PrismaClient (we do) and prefer pooling in prod.
#
# Example shape (NOT a real credential):
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DBNAME?sslmode=require"

# DIRECT (non-pooled) connection — Prisma MIGRATIONS only (`directUrl` in
# schema.prisma). Locally this is the same container as DATABASE_URL, which has
# no pooler. In production DATABASE_URL is Neon's POOLED host and this is not:
# a transaction-mode pooler cannot run DDL or hold the advisory locks that
# `migrate deploy` takes.
#
# Optional for the APP (packages/config marks it optional, and the running
# services never use it), but REQUIRED wherever migrations run — with directUrl
# in the schema the Prisma CLI refuses to start when it is unset.
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@DIRECT_HOST:5432/DBNAME?sslmode=require"
